# CODEOWNERS — required reviewers per area
#
# Syntax: <path-pattern>  @user-or-team  [@another-user]
# More-specific patterns override less-specific ones (last match wins per GitHub).
# Keep this file in sync with /docs/ownership.md.
#
# This fork is a solo repo (T-003): every area is owned by @drewcurley, required
# approvals are 0 (GitHub forbids self-approval) and code-owner review is off, so
# this file routes review requests but blocks nothing (ADOPTING.md § 5). When a
# second maintainer joins, give the gate files a second owner and turn it on.

# Repo-wide default — at least one human approver required on every PR
*                               @drewcurley

# Project conventions and process
/AGENTS.md                      @drewcurley
/CLAUDE.md                      @drewcurley
/.claude/                       @drewcurley
/.github/                       @drewcurley

# Gate files (starter T-014). A PR build runs the PR's own pipeline YAML, so these files
# define the check the PR is judged by: changing them needs the people who own the
# gates. In this solo fork that's one owner; once there are two, every gate line must
# name both (last match wins, so no line may drop one).
# `*` above already requires a default reviewer; this routes gate changes further.
/azure-pipelines.yml            @drewcurley
/scripts/ci-*.sh                @drewcurley
/scripts/requirements-ci.*      @drewcurley
/.githooks/                     @drewcurley
/.placeholder-allow             @drewcurley
/.gitattributes                 @drewcurley
/.github/CODEOWNERS             @drewcurley

# Tasks ledger — DRI sets stay loose, but require any DRI to approve
/tasks/                         @drewcurley

# Living docs — unanimous-consensus rule applies; CODEOWNERS adds a human review gate on top
/docs/                          @drewcurley
/docs/architecture.md           @drewcurley
/docs/stack.md                  @drewcurley
/docs/data-model.md             @drewcurley
/docs/api.md                    @drewcurley
/docs/ux.md                     @drewcurley
/docs/testing.md                @drewcurley
/docs/deployment.md             @drewcurley
/docs/runbooks/                 @drewcurley
/docs/decisions/                @drewcurley
/docs/ownership.md              @drewcurley
/docs/onboarding.md             @drewcurley

